 "_doc": "Bilingual 'REKENINGSTAAT - STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT / BELASTINGFAKTUUR - TAX INVOICE' print: masthead with the municipality's own 'VAT REG NO', ACCOUNTNO, STATEMENT DATE (yyyymmdd), bank block naming JB Marks Local Municipality, property valuation, DEPOSIT block, a METER READINGS table (READING PERIOD | METER NO | CURRENT READING + Rdg/Int code | PREV. READING | CONSUMPTION KWh, CT factor already applied), then the transaction list (left) beside a per-service summary (ELECTR./WATER/SEWER/REFUSE: B/F BAL, CREDITS, DEBITS, BALANCE), sub-totals, 'VAT included @ n%' and GRAND TOTAL. Three electricity meters on one account, each billed as one 'ELECTRICITY-PRIVATE <tariff>' energy line; every amount is VAT-INCLUSIVE and nothing ex-VAT is printed. total_ex_vat_r (= standard_r, single band) is therefore derived: electricity incl / (1 + rate), the rate built from the printed 'VAT included @ n%' (concat of the printed '.' and '15', since the engine has no literals or division) and the division done as x(1-r)(1+r^2)(1+r^4)(1+r^8) with mul/sub/sum (error < 1e-9 R). Meters joined with '/', kWh = sum of the meters' consumption; individual readings are not mapped (three meters). The READING PERIOD prints the same date twice; mapped as printed. IDENTITY jbm_ex_via_vat_r = electricity incl - (printed VAT - the VAT share of the WATER/SEWER/REFUSE summary debits): within 1c on 10/10 (cent rounding of the bill's VAT). Also ELECTR. summary DEBITS = sum of electricity lines. 10/10 routed, 0 checks. Fingerprint: municipality VAT number + name."
}